+# Eight separately indexed BIGINT virtual columns are required to exceed the
+# old update-buffer capacity. TABLE_SHARE::reclength accounts for one packed
+# copy of every SQL column value, including virtual columns. For this schema it
+# is 62 bytes with seven virtual columns and 70 bytes with eight virtual columns
+# (4 bytes for c0, 8 bytes for each BIGINT virtual column, and 2 bytes for the
+# null bitmap/preamble).
+#
+# The old update buffer was reclength + max_key_length + MAX_REF_PARTS * 3.
+# max_key_length is 9 bytes for one nullable BIGINT index and does not grow with
+# the number of secondary indexes, so the old buffer was 119 bytes for seven
+# virtual indexes and 127 bytes for eight. Updating c0 changes every indexed
+# virtual column, and calc_row_difference() keeps both new and old packed BIGINT
+# values for each one: 4 + (N * 2 * 8) bytes. Seven virtual indexes need 116
+# bytes and still leave 3 bytes free, while eight need 132 bytes and overflow
+# the old allocation by 5 bytes.
